HeaderName.description:
Native label forms sufficient for this bounded scalar header family.
Unencodable text is identified without losing its native ordinal matches;
successful schemas requiring it remain unfinished, after prior guards.

NativeValue.description:
One complete logical JSON-like value before native presentation or model
JSON escaping. Numeric bits and Unicode points preserve native values;
no model field, default, task choice or normalization rule is encoded here.

FrameReferenceValues.description:
Actual complete-task or per-batch reference values at their distinct
reached astype(str) positions. Numeric keys retain the core-owned cast;
a native failure has no invented Arrow success value or diagnostic cast.

request_id.description:
The id this call carries in its `metadata.request_id`, which the
host draws for each call, as [`ForecastStep::request_id`];
`materialize` writes none.

The id this question's call carries, as [`ForecastStep::request_id`];
`materialize` writes none, and `predict` refuses a later candidate's
question without one (`INVALID_REQUEST`).

text_times.description:
How the source reads a time it stores as text (register DT-7);
`None` declares no reading, and the core refuses to read text times
from it (`UNSUPPORTED_REQUEST`, rule `text_times`).
